    feat: deploy-readiness — working SHAP XAI, portable config, complete requirements
    
    SHAP explainer (ENABLE_SHAP_XAI path) actually works now:
    - Old wiring built a fresh UNTRAINED GCN per request and handed it to
      shap.DeepExplainer, which crashed instantly (the GCN forward takes
      (x, edge_index); SHAP calls model(x)) — and would have explained
      random weights even without the crash.
    - New engine: built once per process (thread-safe for Daphne's sync
      thread pool), over the TRAINED weights in models_data/gcn_dsa.pth,
      with an adapter fixing the forward signature and a lock around SHAP
      computation. DeepExplainer is probed for silent all-zero attributions
      (torch-geometric layers trigger this) and falls back to
      GradientExplainer; the background spans the feature range because the
      trained model has dead-ReLU regions near the origin where gradients
      are legitimately zero.
    - SHAP output normalized to the SAME schema the frontend reads for the
      heuristic path (shap_values/dominant_factor/success_probability), and
      ANY failure falls back to the heuristic — /code/next/ can never 500
      over explainability. Verified live: distinct, non-degenerate
      attributions per user profile; success prob 21.7% (weak) vs 81.2%
      (strong) from the trained GCN.
    - tensor_builder is now torch-free (returns a plain feature list); the
      SHAP boundary converts. The default heuristic path no longer needs
      PyTorch loaded at all.
    
    Deploy blockers fixed:
    - requirements.txt listed 9 packages; the app imports ~25. A fresh
      environment could not boot. Now complete and pinned from the working
      venv, with the heavy ML extras (torch/shap/transformers) marked.
    - Frontend had 14 hardcoded localhost:8000 / 127.0.0.1:8000 URLs (11
      HTTP + 3 WebSocket) across 12 files; all now use VITE_API_URL /
      VITE_WS_URL with local fallbacks (.env.example added).
    - Judge0 host header was hardcoded to judge0-ce while settings defaulted
      to judge0-extra-ce; both host and base URL now come from
      JUDGE0_API_HOST (matches the existing .env).
    - STATIC_ROOT added (collectstatic); production refuses to boot on the
      well-known dev SECRET_KEY; channel layer upgrades to Redis when
      REDIS_URL is set and channels-redis is installed (in-memory only works
      for a single Daphne process).
    
    Tests: 30/30 passing (new: SHAP payload schema guarantee under
    ENABLE_SHAP_XAI). Frontend production build verified.

